course: dictionary
lesson: 9826
title: Sweetly: kind, sly or perfect
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Sweetly» is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Its meaning depends on the words around it. «Sitting by the driver, Toad asks sweetly if she may try driving, just to tell her friends.» Asking sweetly sounds polite and gentle, but the words «just to tell her friends» are a clue that Toad may be up to something.
explain: The same word can mean different things. A «sweetly scented» flower has a nice smell. A ball «struck sweetly» in football or cricket is hit perfectly. «Sang sweetly» means the song sounded lovely. Read the whole sentence to choose the right meaning.
explain: Be careful with the sly meaning. When someone «smiles sweetly» while planning a trick, the kindness is only pretend. Ask yourself: does this person seem to be up to something? If so, sweetly means pretending to be nice.
explain: Alice's puppy story shows a gentle, coaxing voice without using the word sweetly: «An enormous puppy reaches out a paw to her; Alice speaks to it in a coaxing tone, but she is afraid it might be hungry and eat her.» Her voice is soft and sweet, but her fear shows that the puppy may not be safe.
fact: «Sweetly» is an adverb: it tells you how someone does something.
fact: «Sweetly» means in a kind, gentle and pleasant way.
fact: «Sweetly» can also mean with a nice, sweet sound or smell, as in «sweetly scented».
fact: «Sweetly» can mean smoothly and well, as in a ball sweetly struck.
fact: Ironic use: «smiled sweetly» can mean pretending to be nice when you are not.
exercise: «Sitting by the driver, Toad asks sweetly if she may try driving, just to tell her friends.» How does Toad ask? | *Politely and gently, but with a sly plan | Angrily, shouting at the driver | Sadly, with tears in his eyes | Loudly, to wake everyone up
exercise: Flowers that are sweetly scented have what? | A very slow growth | A rude, angry look | *A nice smell | A sharp, loud noise
exercise: In sport talk, a ball hit sweetly means: | *Hit perfectly | Hit into the crowd by mistake | Dropped on the grass | Hit so hard it breaks
test: Alice speaks «in a coaxing tone» to the puppy. What does coaxing tone suggest? | *Gentle and sweet | Fast and rude | Bored and tired | Loud and angry
test: A character «smiles sweetly» while planning a trick. What does sweetly mean here? | Truly kind and happy | *Pretending to be nice | Lost and confused | Sleeping peacefully
exam: Kai says sweetly always means kind and nice, no matter what. Is he right? | Yes, sweetly never means anything else | Yes, and it always means sweet food | No, it can mean pretending to be nice when someone is sly | *No, but only because it can also mean perfectly struck, like a ball
